{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Still you exalt yourself.</b> Like משתבח from the root of סלסלה and תרוממך (Proverbs 4:5). And if it is a doubled peh, it is of the doubled-peh [forms], like סלו לרוכב בערבות (Psalms 68:5), and גלגלתיך (Jeremiah 51:25) like מתגולל (2 Samuel 20:12), also גלו (Joshua 10:10). And Rabbi Marinus said that it means 'strengthens himself,' from the root of מסלות לבית ד' (2 Chronicles 9:11), and in another place it is written מסעד לבית ד' (1 Kings 10:12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Proverbs 4:5 citation appears erroneous; סלסלה and תרוממך occur at Proverbs 4:8. The parenthetical glosses on the Hebrew forms (e.g., 'doubled-peh') follow his terse grammatical shorthand without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:58.498627572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}